WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.910
Going to school in New Orleans in the
early 2000s was dismal, with only one in

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:10.230
four children scoring at their standard
grade level. The City School Board was so

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.160
corrupt that the FBI started an
investigation and eventually put its

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.960
president and 30 others into jail. On top
of this almost all of the teachers were

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.039
organized in unions. This ensured that
even the worst teachers kept their job

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:27.359
for life. Idealistic educators and
politicians tried to change the system

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:30.929
but their efforts were blocked by those
in charge who did everything possible to

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:39.180
keep things as they were. Then things got
worse. In 2005 Katrina, a massive

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.559
hurricane, struck the city and destroyed
virtually everything including all

00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:49.050
schools. As a result, everyone left the
city. Kids stopped going to school. The

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.160
school board lost all of its funding and
the teachers lost their jobs leading to

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:59.460
unions losing all of their members. It
was a true disaster for everyone. In the

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.359
aftermath of Katrina politicians,
bureaucrats and educators saw an

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:06.780
opportunity to finally bring change
upon a system that had previously failed

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:11.310
so many kids in such a miserable way.
Under the leadership of governor

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.479
Kathleen Blanco it was concluded that
while they didn't know the best solution

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:19.229
they did know that the system had to be
created using trial and error and

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:26.580
experimentation. They had an idea: Instead
of running a top-down system of state

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.799
schools, their idea was to allow
independent charter schools to take over.

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:35.250
Charters are schools that are fully
state-funded, free of charge and run by

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:39.420
independent entrepreneurs who follow
their mission. Charter schools hire their

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.110
own teachers and set up their own
curriculums. They often even build their

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:49.049
own facilities and then compete with one
another to attract new students. As a

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:53.520
result of this bold effort to reform
a lot of philanthropists and nonprofit

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.450
organizations invested into New Orleans
education and hundreds of charter

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:01.560
schools opened up. Parents and their
children suddenly had a lot of choices

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:06.360
in picking schools aligned with their
ideas regarding quality education. The

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.940
schools that didn't attract enough
children closed down again.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:16.610
in 2019, 15 years later, almost half of
all students performed at grade level.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:20.640
High school graduation rates increased
and college outcomes became

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.480
significantly better. New Orleans had
become the first large American city

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:30.450
that does not operate a single
traditional public school. The story of

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.050
New Orleans schools shows what is
possible when old structures break down

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.490
and people have no choice but to leave a
damaged system. Good people who were

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:43.200
stuck in a bad system then get an
opportunity to start fresh. Parents and

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.440
children have the opportunity to choose
for themselves the type of schools that

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:53.310
they believe in. How are the schools
organized in your country? Do you think

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.720
that a reform of that system would
benefit the students? If so, what change

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.130
would you propose?

